      <profiles>
        <profile name="Trolls" id="932d-5908-178e-d0af" hidden="false" typeId="939e-319b-8950-616f" typeName="Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Type" typeId="3087-9431-0004-e975">Infantry</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Attacks" typeId="ce3c-e837-0a09-dba6">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Hits" typeId="f51a-b726-0fbe-0569">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Armour" typeId="1b25-0ce9-c54e-e226">5+</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Command" typeId="73c2-d4e8-04e7-dcbc">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Unit size" typeId="72b4-6deb-0f8e-7f27">3</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Trolls" id="50ac-d125-c98c-eb82" hidden="false" typeId="a5d3-6ea8-6425-5123" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="bc69-55f2-6b4e-18e7">A unit of trolls may never advance more than 10cm after combat.

Even though Trolls are quite stupid they have uncanny sense of smell. This sense of smell allows a unit of trolls to trace a LOS through friendly units to the enemy.


A unit of Trolls will always use initiative to charge the closest enemy unit within 20cm, even if an unengaged friendly unit lies between the Trolls and their victims. When a unit of trolls is forced to charge an enemy unit and their path takes them through an unengaged friendly unit, a burst through is performed on the unit the Trolls were forced to move through. Remember this rule applies to unengaged friendly units only.


Trolls will never trace a LOS through, charge through, or displace a friendly unit already in contact with the enemy.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
