            <characteristic name="Hits" typeId="f51a-b726-0fbe-0569">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Armour" typeId="1b25-0ce9-c54e-e226">0</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Command" typeId="73c2-d4e8-04e7-dcbc">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Unit size" typeId="72b4-6deb-0f8e-7f27">3</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Wargs" id="105b-6a57-550f-74b1" hidden="false" typeId="a5d3-6ea8-6425-5123" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="bc69-55f2-6b4e-18e7">Wargs are able to move over or into any wooded or mountainous terrain features in the same way as infantry. This does not allow them to claim the defended status. 

Wargs cannot be brigaded with units of other troops, only with other Wargs.

A Warg unit which scores more hits in the first round of a combat than the enemy will automatically strike 1 more Attack per stand before the combat result is worked out. Resolve these attacks as normal and then work out the results. 

Wargs must always pursue retreating enemy where possible and must advance if they are able to do so. 

Note that these rules apply only to Warg units – not to characters that ride Wargs.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
